<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis says FDA approves Femara.</title>
<headline>Novartis says FDA approves Femara.</headline>
<text>
<p>BASLE, Switzerland, July 31 - Pharmaceutical and life sciences group Novartis AG said the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) had given it clearance to market Femara, a new medication for treating advanced breast cancer.</p>
<p>&quot;Femara offers the thousands of postmenopausal women with advanced breast cancer an important therapy that may effectively shrink tumours or slow the progression of the disease in some cases,&quot; Novartis said in a statement.</p>
</text>
